# UI system

Material UI is the design-system foundation. Emotion is used only through MUI. Do not add Tailwind, shadcn/ui, or another visual system.

UI architecture:

```text
MUI foundation
-> ERP theme
-> ERP primitives
-> ERP layout components
-> ERP patterns
-> feature components
-> pages
```

Every Material UI import belongs in `@erp/ui`. `apps/web`, including features, `shared/`, and `widgets/`, does not import `@mui/*` or `@emotion/*`. It composes `@erp/ui`.

Reusable primitives, layout, patterns, and the ERP theme belong in `@erp/ui`. Inside that package, do not add an empty wrapper around a MUI component. Add a wrapper only when it provides ERP-wide behavior, defaults, accessibility, variants, styling, or API consistency. Theme overrides are preferred when they are enough.

Future primitives include Button, TextField, Select, Checkbox, Dialog, Drawer, Tabs, Chip, Tooltip, Menu, Table, Autocomplete, and date controls.

Future layout includes Page, PageContent, PageHeader, Stack, Grid, FormGrid, Section, and Container.

Future patterns include DataTable, FilterBar, Pagination, EntityHeader, EntityForm, FormSection, EmptyState, ErrorState, LoadingState, ConfirmDialog, and PermissionGate.

Do not add an empty MUI wrapper inside `@erp/ui`. A wrapper must add behavior, defaults, accessibility, variants, styling, or a stable API.

Before creating a generic UI component:

1. Inspect MUI itself.
2. Inspect `@erp/ui` primitives.
3. Inspect `@erp/ui` layout.
4. Inspect `@erp/ui` patterns.
5. Only then introduce a new abstraction.

Styling hierarchy:

```text
theme tokens
-> theme component overrides and variants
-> reusable @erp/ui components
-> MUI sx or styled for local exceptions
```

Prefer semantic palette tokens such as `primary`, `error`, `background.default`, `background.paper`, `text.primary`, `text.secondary`, and `divider`.

Prefer `theme.spacing(...)` and `theme.breakpoints.up(...)` or `theme.breakpoints.down(...)`. Use responsive props and breakpoint objects instead of custom pixel logic.

Feature components must not repeatedly invent colors, spacing scales, typography, breakpoints, radii, elevations, generic loading states, generic tables, or generic form layout.

`@erp/ui` must not import `apps/web` or `apps/api`.

`@erp/ui` stays free of React Hook Form and free of ERP domain types. Generic field adapters live in `apps/web/src/shared/forms`. Feature forms bind them inside the feature.

Repeated page chrome (`PageLayout`, `PageHeader`, `PageContent`) belongs in `@erp/ui` layout so features do not copy margins, widths, and action alignment.

A data grid is a later decision. Do not build a custom grid framework before an existing library is tried against a real ERP table. The grid engine must not know what an invoice or customer is.
